Title: Segmenter identity and the PDF-path-vs-seg/1 selection rule
Created: 2026-09-01
Author: claude
Blocked-by: 0557

--- log ---
2026-09-01T13:31Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

Child of tracker 0557, the natural last child -- it is the integration
point and needs both a working seg/1 (0028) and at least tier 1 (0560) to
have something to select between. `SPEC.md` §5.2.1 (stage keys) already
fixes the shape: the chunk key is `(text_hash, segmenter id+version,
chunker id+geometry)` -- "the segmenter lives inside the chunker key,
exactly as the boundary ruling directs." A second segmenter needs its own
identity string distinct from `seg/1`, or a segmenter-bump re-embed would
silently conflate two different segmentation methods under one key.

## Actions

1. Name the new segmenter's identity string (e.g. `seg/2` or similar --
   pick something that reads unambiguously in logs and chunk keys next to
   `seg/1`).
2. Record the selection rule: PDF path attempted when the length trigger
   (0559) fires AND attachment file access (0558) succeeds; falls through
   to seg/1 when the trigger doesn't fire, file access fails, tier 1 finds
   no outline AND tier 2 is low-confidence.
3. Confirm the re-embed-on-segmenter-bump behavior (SPEC.md §2.1) holds
   correctly across BOTH segmenters -- switching an attachment from seg/1
   to the PDF path (or back, on a PDF-access regression) must re-embed,
   not silently keep stale chunks under a mismatched key.

## Test

- A document that qualifies for the PDF path on one run and falls back to
  seg/1 on a later run (simulated file-access failure) -- assert the chunk
  key changes and re-embedding actually happens, not a stale mix.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] segmenter identity string chosen and recorded (SPEC.md and/or a
      DECISIONS.md note, per the chain -- this is a design-number change,
      not a code-only one)
- [ ] selection rule implemented, matching the fallthrough order in 0557
- [ ] segmenter-switch re-embed behavior tested
